{"shortDescription":"The ninth edition of the BW Sustainable World Awards 2026 recognises organisations and individuals advancing climate action, resource stewardship, innovation and responsible businessClimate action, circularity, water conservation and cleaner mobility feature prominently in this year’s roll of honou…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The ninth edition of the BW Sustainable World Awards 2026 recognises organisations and individuals advancing climate action, resource stewardship, innovation and responsible business"]},{"type":"p","children":["Climate action, circularity, water conservation and cleaner mobility feature prominently in this year’s roll of honour, alongside sustainability reporting, responsible business and individual leadership. The BW Sustainable World Awards 2026 recognise this work through 40 honours across 16 categories, comprising gold, silver and bronze awards as well as jury mentions."]},{"type":"p","children":["An initiative of BW Businessworld and BW Sustainability World, the awards seek to identify organisations and individuals demonstrating genuine sustainability impact, leadership, innovation and credibility. The emphasis is on contributions that merit recognition within their respective categories, supported by evidence of meaningful change."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Evaluating The Impact"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The 2026 selection process reached more than 500 organisations and received 160 nominations. Of these, 100 were screened and shortlisted for jury evaluation. The evaluation framework set out six parameters including impact, innovation, credibility, scale and relevance, long-term value and category fit. Jurors were asked to consider measurable outcomes, the evidence supporting claims, the potential for wider adoption and the creation of sustained environmental, social or business value. Under the framework, nominees receiving a ‘yes’ verdict progressed to collective jury deliberation to determine gold, silver or bronze recognition."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["The Jury Behind The Selection"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The jury was chaired by Dr Bhaskar Chatterjee, former Secretary to the Government of India and former Director General of the Indian Institute of Corporate Affairs."]},{"type":"p","children":["Members included Dr Vibha Dhawan of The Energy and Resources Institute, Nisheeth Srivastava of AIA Group, Dr G Sridhar, former Director General of the Sardar Swaran Singh National Institute of Bio-Energy, sustainability and sustainable finance board advisor Chandni Khosla, Shalini Goyal Bhalla of the International Council for Circular Economy, Sudhir Mishra of Trust Legal, and author, board member and corporate advisor Srinath Sridharan."]},{"type":"p","children":["The panel also included Chandni Raina of the Ministry of Finance, Dr Ashvini Kumar of Shakti Sustainable Energy Foundation, Dr Sameer Joshi of the Indian Plastics Institute, Shantanu Roy, formaer Chief Sustainability Officer of GAIL, and Shalabh Tandon and Rajesh Miglani of the International Finance Corporation."]},{"type":"p","children":["Completing the panel were Jatinder Jay Cheema of Chambers of Jay Cheema, Dr Srikanta K Panigrahi of the Indian Institute of Sustainable Development, Nidhi Sarin of the Global Energy Allaiance for People \u0026 Planet and Vikram Kotru of FICCI."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"i","children":["The complete list of winners, their award categories and levels of recognition follows"]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["S. No"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["CATEGORY"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["WINNER"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["VERDICT"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["1"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["C